# Netlify headers file.
#
# `output: "export"` copies everything in public/ into out/, which is Netlify's
# publish directory — so this file ships as out/_headers and Netlify applies it.
#
# These values are intentionally IDENTICAL to the [[headers]] block in
# netlify.toml. Netlify's docs do not state which source wins when both define
# the same header, so keeping them in agreement means precedence never matters.
# If you edit one, edit the other (and vercel.json, which mirrors both).
#
# Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy + Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy are load-bearing:
# they make the page cross-origin isolated, which enables SharedArrayBuffer and
# lets src/lib/ffmpeg.worker.ts load the multi-threaded FFmpeg core. Without
# them exports silently fall back to single-threaded and get much slower.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
